Description

Scenario: An intelligence agency recovered a suspicious document from a compromised workstation during an internal security investigation. The document allegedly contains classified operational details and a hidden recovery token used by a rogue insider group. Analysts discovered that the file is password protected. The attacker intentionally left misleading clues and fake credentials in nearby files to delay investigators. Your objective is to recover the correct password protecting the document and open the encrypted file.

Tasks:
    a) Analyze the provided files and extract the password hash from Secret.docx
    b) Crack the password and open the encrypted document
    c) Retrieve the flag hidden inside the document
Provided Files: 
    a) Readme_recovery.docx — Recovery notes left by the Operations team
    b) Secret.docx — Password-protected classified document

Deliverables: 
    a) Flag format: PASSWORD						                         25 pts
    b) Walk through document:
        a. Steps / commands to recover hash & document  hash	 3 pts
        b. Attack applied/ commands used to recover password        5 pts
        c. Tools used 							                       	 1 pt
        d. Flag CTF {PASSWORD}					                        	 1 pt
